From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:58:45 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 070/207] In-model runner: inline decimals and fractions
 abstain in a Python-float reply

A code cell or a float cue (float, Decimal(, sum(, round(, 0.1+0.2) within TF_DSV41_RUNNER_FLOAT_WINDOW
tokens (default 512) marks an inline span with . or / as float context; the runner abstains (context).
Integer-only spans stay exact everywhere.
---
 zig/src/core/runner.zig      |  7 +++++
 zig/src/core/runner_api.zig  |  2 +-
 zig/src/core/runner_scan.zig | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 zig/src/core/runner_test.zig | 13 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 77 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

